useCases.userJourney:
Access to a protected Agency web service requires two independent conditions met in sequence. First, the contractor's verifiable credential: a cryptographically signed document proving current affiliation with a trusted contractor organization is checked via Turing Space and must be valid, unexpired, and unrevoked at access time. Only after this credential-based verification succeeds can the user proceed to Hideez's passwordless authentication layer. Access is granted only when both conditions are satisfied; an invalid, expired, or revoked credential blocks access.

Workflow: 
(1) IT admin issues a VC for the user via the Hideez Workforce ID portal; 
(2) user receives a confirmation email and adds the VC to the Paradym Wallet app by scanning the email's QR code; 
(3) user registers a passwordless authentication method (Hideez mobile app, platform Passkey, or external FIDO2 key) in Hideez IdP, linked to the VC; 
(4) a new user account is automatically created in on-premises Active Directory; 
(5) user signs in passwordlessly to SSO-configured web services via Hideez IdP; 
(6) if the VC is expired or revoked by IT admin, the user's access to web services is blocked.
